{
  "title": "Dua of Imam al-Kazim (a.s.) after Asr for Imam Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ",
  "data": "اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ الْاَوَّلُ وَالْاٰخِرُ وَالظَّاهِرُ وَالْبَاطِنُ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTAL AWWALO WAL AAKHERO WAZ ZAAHERO WAL BAATENO\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You, the First and the Last, the Manifest and the Hidden.\nوَاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَيْكَ زِيَادَةُ الْاَشْيَاۤءِ وَنُقْصَانُهَا\nWA ANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA ELAYKA ZEYAADATUL ASHYAAA-E WA NUQSAANOHAA\nAnd You are Allah, there is no god but You; to You belongs the increase of all things and their decrease.\nوَاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ خَلَقْتَ خَلْقَكَ بِغَيْرِ مَعُوْنَةٍ مِّنْ غَيْرِكَ وَلَا حَاجَةٍ اِلَيْهِمْ\nWA ANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA KHALAQTA KHALQAKA BE-GHAYRE MA-O'NATIM MIN GHAYREKA WA LAA HAAJATIN ELAYHIM\nAnd You are Allah, there is no god but You; You created Your creation without help from anyone other than You, and without any need of them.\nوَاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ مِنْكَ الْمَشِيَّةُ وَاِلَيْكَ الْبَدَاۤءُ\nWA ANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA MINKAL MASHIYYATO WA ELAYKAL BADAAA-O\nAnd You are Allah, there is no god but You; from You is the Will, and to You belongs the change of decree (bada').\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ قَبْلَ الْقَبْلِ وَخَالِقُ الْقَبْلِ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA QABLAL QABLE WA KHAALEQUL QABLE\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; before all that is before, and the Creator of the before.\nوَاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ بَعْدَ الْبَعْدِ وَخَالِقُ الْبَعْدِ\nWA ANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA BA'DAL BA'DE WA KHAALEQUL BA'DE\nAnd You are Allah, there is no god but You; after all that is after, and the Creator of the after.\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ تَمْحُوْ مَا تَشَاۤءُ وَتُثْبِتُ وَعِنْدَكَ اُمُّ الْكِتَابِ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA TAMHOO MAA TASHAAA-O WA TUSBETO WA I'NDAKA UMMUL KETAABE\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; You erase what You will and You confirm, and with You is the Mother of the Book.\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ غَايَةُ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَّوَارِثُهٗ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA GHAAYATO KULLE SHAY-IW WA WAARESOHU\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; the End of every thing and its Inheritor.\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ لَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْكَ الدَّقِيْقُ وَلَا الْجَلِيْلُ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA LAA YA'ZOBO A'NKAD DAQEEQO WA LAL JALEELO\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; nothing escapes You, neither the minute nor the great.\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ لَا تَخْفٰى عَلَيْكَ اللُّغَاتُ وَلَا تَتَشَابَهُ عَلَيْكَ الْاَصْوَاتُ\nANTAL LAAHO LAAA ELAAHA ILLAAA ANTA LAA TAKHFAA A'LAYKAL LOGHAATO WA LAA TATASHAABAHO A'LAYKAL ASWAATO\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; no language is hidden from You, and no voices are confused for You.\nكُلَّ يَوْمٍ اَنْتَ فِيْ شَاْنٍ لَا يَشْغَلُكَ شَاْنٌ عَنْ شَاْنٍ\nKULLA YAWMIN ANTA FEE SHAANIL LAA YASHGHALOKA SHAANUN A'N SHAANIN\nEvery day You are in a (new) affair; no affair distracts You from another affair.\nعَالِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَاَخْفٰى دَيَّانُ يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ مُدَبِّرُ الْاُمُوْرِ\nA'ALEMUL GHAYBE WA AKHFAA DAYYAANO YAWMID DEENE MODABBERUL OMOORE\nKnower of the unseen and what is more hidden, Judge of the Day of Judgment, Disposer of all affairs,\nبَاعِثُ مَنْ فِي الْقُبُوْرِ مُحْيِي الْعِظَامِ وَهِيَ رَمِيْمٌ\nBAA-E'SO MAN FIL QOBOORE MOHYIL E'ZAAME WA HEYA RAMEEMUN\nResurrector of those in the graves, Giver of life to the bones when they have decayed.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الْمَكْنُوْنِ الْمَخْزُوْنِ الْحَيِّ الْقَيُّوْمِ الَّذِيْ لَا يَخِيْبُ مَنْ سَاَلَكَ بِهٖ\nAS-ALOKA BISMEKAL MAKNOONIL MAKHZOONIL HAYYIL QAYYOOMIL LAZEE LAA YAKHEEBO MAN SA-ALAKA BEHI\nI ask You by Your hidden, treasured Name, the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting, by which no one who asks You is ever disappointed,\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A'LAA MOHAMMADIW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nI ask You to send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تُعَجِّلَ فَرَجَ الْمُنْتَقِمِ لَكَ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكَ\nWA AN TO-A'JJELA FARAJAL MUNTAQEME LAKA MIN A-A'DAAA-EKA\nand to hasten the relief of the one who will take vengeance for You upon Your enemies,\nوَاَنْجِزْ لَهٗ مَا وَعَدْتَّهٗ يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nWA ANJIZ LAHU MAA WA-A'TTAHU YAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME\nand fulfil for him what You have promised him, O Possessor of Majesty and Honour.",
  "merits": "It is mentioned in Falah al-Sa'il (Sayyid Ibn Tawus) among the important supplications to be recited after the Asr (afternoon) prayer, following the example of Imam Musa ibn Ja'far al-Kazim (a.s.) in his supplication dedicated to Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.).\nYahya ibn al-Fadl al-Nawfali narrates: I entered upon Abu al-Hasan Musa ibn Ja'far (a.s.) in Baghdad as he finished the Asr prayer. He raised his hands towards the heavens and I heard him recite this supplication.\nYahya said: I asked, \"Who is the one being prayed for?\" He replied, \"That is al-Mahdi from the family of Muhammad (s.a.w.a.).\" Then he said: \"May my father be sacrificed for him - of wide belly, joined eyebrows, slender shins, broad shoulders and a wheat-coloured complexion, tinged with a pallor from staying awake at night. May my father be sacrificed for the one who spends his nights watching the stars, prostrating and bowing. May my father be sacrificed for the one who, in the way of Allah, fears no blame of any blamer - the lamp in the darkness. May my father be sacrificed for the one who will rise by the command of Allah.\""
}
